  abstract: >-
    On a 600-scenario corpus spanning three policy rules, 155 adversarial scenarios across
    eight prompt-injection techniques, 60 compound and 30 boundary cases, constraining the
    output format without requiring the reasoning step produces the least safe evaluator of
    the three conditions tested, approving 46.2% of proposals the policy would block or route
    to review. The full schema cuts that to 23.5% and raises hard-denial accuracy from 62.5%
    to 90.8%, but still approves 6 of 208 irreversible actions.
